invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_mont_mul returns without wiping its running sum, so
  the last product before its subtraction and the last round's multiple
  of the modulus stay in the dead frame after every multiplication a
  signature makes. No output changes, so no vector notices.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test copies the stack below one signature and finds
  two words of a half of the signature there, which the last
  multiplication of an exponentiation left.

--- old
    // the product, and the last round's u above it.
    ct_wipe(t, (k + 2) * sizeof(uint64_t));
--- new
    // the product, and the last round's u above it.
